<title>PORTUGAL: Strong demand for Portugal's BES.</title>
<headline>Strong demand for Portugal's BES.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Portuguese bank Banco Espirito Santo experienced firm demand in high volume on Lisbon bourse as the share adjusted to the general rise in the market, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand for BES is related to the rise of the market and the fact that this share had not recovered as much as other banking shares,&quot; one operator said.</p>
<p>BES stood at 2,580 escudos, up 61, in volume of 399,262 shares at 1508 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
